Licence of this repository

1. Original work. Text, prompts, checklists, eval cases, templates, scripts and
   documentation written for this repository are licensed under the Creative
   Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0):
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Attribution: "AI: a compilation of AI harnesses" by Aman Upadhyay,
   https://github.com/aman161upadhyay/AI
   This covers every file whose authorship is ours, including README.md,
   FOR-AMAN.md and SOURCE.md files that sit inside folders that also hold
   third-party material.

2. Third-party work keeps its own licence. A file is third-party when the
   SOURCE.md in its folder (or the nearest SOURCE.md above it) lists it as
   vendored, adapted or converted. The upstream licence text is reproduced in
   the LICENSE or NOTICE file next to it, with one exception: where the
   copyright holder declares a licence but publishes no licence file (as of
   2026-10-25 only vercel-labs/agent-skills, README "License: MIT"), the
   folder carries LICENSE-NOTE.md with the declaration, its URL and commit,
   and the standard text of the declared licence for reference; no copyright
   notice is invented. Modified third-party files carry a modification notice
   after their front matter. Examples:
   - 01-skills-library/anthropic/ and the Anthropic skills under
     03-agents/design-agent/skills/vendored/anthropic/: Apache-2.0.
   - 01-skills-library/community/<owner>__<repo>/: the licence recorded in that
     folder's SOURCE.md (MIT, Apache-2.0, CC0-1.0, CC BY 4.0 or CC BY-SA 4.0).
   - 02-prompts/fabric-patterns/: MIT (Daniel Miessler's Fabric).
   - 06-reference-library/papers/ and 06-reference-library/figures/: the
     authors' CC BY 4.0 grant for Clark, Martin and Mahowald (2026); our
     summary block inside the paper file is covered by section 1.

3. Share-alike material is isolated. CC BY-SA 4.0 material lives only in
   folders whose name or SOURCE.md marks it as share-alike:
   06-reference-library/articles/wikipedia-signs-of-ai-writing-cc-by-sa/,
   01-skills-library/community/trailofbits__skills/, the Trail of Bits skills
   under 03-agents/security-agent/skills/vendored/, and the OWASP-derived
   authorization reference under 03-agents/security-agent/skills/vendored/sentry/.
   Derivatives of those files must be shared under the same licence.

4. Linked, not copied. Sources whose licence did not permit redistribution,
   or that had no licence, are linked and described in our own words; nothing
   from them is reproduced here beyond short quotations with attribution.

If a file's status is unclear, the nearest SOURCE.md decides; if there is
none, the file is original work under section 1.
